  "limitations": [
    "All measurements are milliseconds, desktop Chrome at native CPU speed; no 4x CPU throttling. Five repetitions per combination are indicative and provide no production percentile or statistical confidence interval.",
    "The harness mounts the real React cashflow page with synthetic auth/profile/data-hook adapters and esbuild test-only worker URL/diagnostics instrumentation. Live loading, server/network, surrounding application shell and real business data are excluded.",
    "elapsedMs includes the requested action and harness wait-until-ready checks (including animation-frame waits and, for some operations, DOM reading/hash work). It is neither isolated computation time nor total page-load time.",
    "The burst scenario sends five changes with a deliberate 16 ms wait after every change. Its elapsed duration includes those scheduled waits and settling; it is not the latency of a single user interaction.",
    "medianMaxFrameGapMs is the median across five per-trial maximum requestAnimationFrame intervals. The gap window also includes setup/cleanup frames outside elapsedMs. It is not an INP measurement, dropped-frame count or precise paint latency; approximately 16.7 ms values reflect the display/browser frame cadence.",
    "Timer delay measures one setTimeout(0) callback scheduled at action start, not continuous responsiveness; it may fire before later expensive work.",
    "Long-task entries cover only the browser main thread, filtered by task start time within elapsedMs. Worker computation is intentionally excluded; tasks starting outside the interval can also be excluded despite overlap.",
    "Execution diagnostics are snapshots at trial completion. All 50 large-portfolio work trials show one active worker and no recorded fallback/pending; all 150 trial records contain zero fallback. Forced fallback is verified separately and is not part of timing trials.",
    "The 36 standard correctness records compare visible UI semantics with baseline across 12 scenarios and three portfolio sizes; the runner additionally checks the opened combined-view month for each size. The 37th record explicitly verifies forced-fallback overview and month detail. These records do not constitute 37 independent month-detail or internal-numeric comparisons.",
    "The final 1000-contract initial action completes 16.7 ms later (250.1 to 266.8 ms) in the work median even though its largest frame-gap median falls from 183.4 to 16.8 ms. Supported conclusion is smoother main-thread behavior in this synthetic case; do not promise faster total loading or improved production INP.",
    "Native Next/Turbopack production bundling and browser worker execution were verified separately in next-worker-runtime.json; the UI performance measurements themselves remain the esbuild synthetic harness."
  ],
